<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFramework>net10.0-windows</TargetFramework>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
    <Platforms>x64</Platforms>
    <PlatformTarget>x64</PlatformTarget>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.NET.Test.Sdk" Version="17.14.1" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit" Version="2.9.3" />
    <!--
      Headless Avalonia, so a pane provider can be constructed in a test. Nothing did, and it
      showed: a KeyGesture.Parse that throws made the file-browser pane impossible to create at all
      and shipped anyway; the address bar read a control from a background thread and had been
      broken since Phase 4; the empty pane's launcher lost half the product. All of it compiled,
      and all of it was found by a person looking at the screen.

      Avalonia.Headless rather than Avalonia.Headless.XUnit, because the xunit integration package
      depends on xunit v3 and this project is on v2; the session is driven directly instead, which
      is what that integration does anyway. Pinned to the same 12.1.2 as Avalonia itself, since a
      mismatch here fails at run time rather than at build.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Avalonia.Headless" Version="12.1.2" />
    <!--
      Dynamic skip. xunit 2.x has no Assert.Skip (that is v3), and a test that silently passes when
      its server is absent would be a green tick proving nothing. Used only by RemoteLiveTests.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Xunit.SkippableFact" Version="1.5.85" />
    <PackageReference Include="xunit.runner.visualstudio" Version="3.1.4" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <Using Include="Xunit" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <ProjectReference Include="..\WinMux.Panes\WinMux.Panes.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\WinMux.Platform.Win32\WinMux.Platform.Win32.csproj" />
    <ProjectReference Include="..\WinMux.Shell\WinMux.Shell.csproj" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
